Native talk is stored as bare prose (Message::assistant(deck_content) at step.rs:670), which fails protocol parse → blanked on the next turn's generate. GBNF answers survive because they're envelope JSON (they hit the compact branch → "Hello\nInvoked tools:"). Billy runs optimize_context = true + assistant_non_json_placeholder = true, so the model is already losing its prior user-facing replies from context. That, not quant, is part of why hosted "forgets what it just said." Cheap fix: exempt native talk turns from the omit-placeholder (compact them instead), keyed off backend or a talk-turn marker.

