§6/§9 direct answers
A — projection & Auto. llm_response_from_engine is the right seam; keep it engine-neutral. tool_choice = Auto in every offered branch, never Required (I confirmed the orchestrator never emits Required; it's engine-capability only) — that correctly dodges the silent-after-tools deadlock. Speech-act (§9.2): keep Auto, add a post-tool talk constraint. Today the only reliable brake before max_tool_rounds = 40 is duplicate-suppression's SuppressOnlyIdlePass. Generalize that existing "force one no-tool pass" into a post-tool policy (after a successful batch that already answers, inject "you have results; answer now" and set tools_needed = false for the next hop). That's the dummy-memory:stage fix — orchestrator + prompt, no Required, no PR#23 rollback. Don't lower max_tool_rounds; that truncates legit multi-tool work.

B — wire. Confirmed: role:tool + provider_call_id cannot reach llama.cpp/Ollama. Consecutive tool frames correctly not coalesced (can_coalesce excludes role == "tool" and any tool_call_id) — correct for LiteLLM, each result needs its own id.

